# ============================================================================
# llm-wiki — Environment Variables
# ============================================================================
# Copy this file:  mkdir -p ~/.config/llm-wiki && cp config/.env.example ~/.config/llm-wiki/.env
# Then fill in the values below. Lines starting with # are comments.
#
# Required vs Optional:
#   Agent authentication     — handled by the selected agent application
#   MINERU_API_TOKEN         — REQUIRED for PDF ingest (free; cloud backend)
#   Review                   — current agent; no additional API key
# ============================================================================


# --- Agent Authentication -------------------------------------------------
# Sign in through your selected agent application (Codex or Claude Code).
# Research review and source audits run there without a separate reviewer API.

# --- MinerU API Token (REQUIRED for PDF ingest) -----------------------------
# What it does:  Vision-language PDF parser. tools/prepare_paper_source.py
#                calls MinerU to turn raw PDFs into structured markdown
#                (frontmatter with sections + figures) that /ingest consumes.
# Used by:       /ingest (every PDF), /init (batch PDF preprocessing)
#
# How to get:    1. Go to https://mineru.net/
#                2. Sign up (free)
#                3. Create an API token in account settings
#                4. Copy the token below
#
# Without token: PDF ingest fails. Local-backend escape hatch:
#                  uv pip install -e ".[local]"
#                (downloads several GB of model weights; no token needed)
MINERU_API_TOKEN=

# Optional: override the API base (default is https://mineru.net/api/v4)
# MINERU_API_BASE=https://mineru.net/api/v4
